From daf47365925490105aa8798a3d24dbefbc6a29c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d-b-c-e <anthony.mason1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 13:33:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 077/124] Built-in force feedback (mvffb): SDL2 haptics on the
 steering axis, replaces the FFB Arcade Plugin

The drivers hand the signed wheel-motor byte (V-Unit WHLCTLZ, Exotica LED-board
offset 0, after gain/slew/clamp) to midv_ffb_write(); a worker thread drives one
signed constant force through SDL2 (SDL_HAPTIC_STEERING_AXIS, infinite length,
update + run per write, stop on zero) the way Cannonball DX / Flycast do. SDL2.dll
is loaded at run time - no import; without it FFB is off and midv_ffb.log says so.
Byte interpretation = the plugin Cruis'n handler (0 stop, |v|/126). Sign measured on
the rig: positive byte pushes right, positive SDL level turns the Moza left, so
level = -sign(byte); MIDV_FFB_INVERT flips. MIDV_FFB / _STRENGTH / _DEVICE /
_HOLD_MS (500 ms release when the game stops writing) / _TEST / _LOG.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mame/midway/midvunit.cpp   |   1 +
 src/mame/midway/midvunit.h     |   3 +
