The collision force RAMPS - byte -25 -40 -67 -80 -103 -113 -126 over about six
frames - then holds near full for seconds. The single-frame jump test therefore
fired once in 463 updates, so the onset thump almost never happened. It now needs
the force to ARRIVE at >=80% of the achievable maximum having RISEN >=40% within
250 ms: 8 thumps in 28 s of racing against that trace, where a rise-only test gave
35 and ordinary steering triggered most of them.

Speed is now written to the FFB trace whenever tracing is on. It was gated on
s_speed_word, which is 0 for every game since the RAM addresses were retired for the
HUD OCR - so a dropout report could never be answered from a support bundle.

